---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { DISCLAIMER } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base title="About — Stillwater Civic Briefing">
  <article class="story">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1>What this paper is</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Stillwater Civic Briefing is a hyper-local paper and a weekly audio episode.
        It covers public meetings, schools, land use, the adult jail book-in report,
        and the week’s calendar for Stillwater, Lake Elmo, Oakdale, Woodbury, Bayport,
        Oak Park Heights, Washington County, Hudson and the Town of Hudson in Wisconsin,
        St. Croix County, the Stillwater Area Public Schools, and the North St. Paul–Maplewood–Oakdale schools.
      </p>
      <p>
        Stories are markdown files in the GitHub repository
        <a href="https://github.com/ncolestock/stillwater-civic-briefing">ncolestock/stillwater-civic-briefing</a>.
        A push to main builds the site in GitHub Actions and publishes it here.
        The laptop does not have to be open.
      </p>
      <p>
        The record comes from agendas, packets, minutes, and official rosters.
        Dollar figures and vote counts appear only when a document states them.
        A scheduled item is described as scheduled. A closed session is described
        by the statutory topic on the agenda. This paper does not scrape other
        newsrooms’ articles.
      </p>
      <p>
        The blotter publishes adult bookings only: the name, the charge as written
        on the official report, the booking date, and the source link. It does not
        publish ages, dates of birth, home addresses, mugshots, medical information,
        or the names of juveniles or of victims of sex crimes.
      </p>
      <p>
        The weekly episode is a reading of that week’s stories. It has no named host.
        Earlier episodes, from before this paper, remain on the <a href="../archive/">archive</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Write to <a href="mailto:nathan0colestock@gmail.com">nathan0colestock@gmail.com</a>.
        A correction is appended to the story with the date. The story is not quietly rewritten.
      </p>
      <p class="disclaimer">{DISCLAIMER}</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
